// Between crossed polars the transmitted intensity goes as sin^2(2(theta - pol)),
// so each defect throws off the dark brushes of the classic schlieren texture,
// and isotropic melt (|Psi| -> 0) goes black because it cannot rotate light.
//
// Left alone, defects pair up and annihilate and the texture anneals to a blank
// uniform field -- dead by ~20s. Kept perpetual by:
//   (1) r(x,y,t), the reduced temperature, drifts through the isotropic-nematic
//       transition, so melt pools open and re-order and every re-ordering
//       quench throws fresh defects (the Kibble-Zurek mechanism);
